{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md; rg -n 'required|optional|ambiguous|frozen|sources|precedence' docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe-targets.json\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_4","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md; rg -n 'required|optional|ambiguous|frozen|sources|precedence' docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe-targets.json\"","aggregated_output":"     1\t# Paid acceptance probe of judging-v12 (design v4, D715; registered before any send)\n     2\t\n     3\t**Alex's ceiling:** $0.50 (D715, \"0.5 美元 (推荐)\"), held by `budget_replay.SharedLedger`, which stops at it.\n     4\t\n     5\t**Frozen inputs:**\n     6\t- `probe-plan.json` (`probe_plan.py`, $0);\n     7\t- `probe-targets.json`: the Part B targets, read from the stored refused answers before any send and never edited after the first.\n     8\t\n     9\t**Model and settings:** poc-v121's rejudging setting (gpt-6-luna, medium effort, 16,000 output tokens), the provider's strict format.\n    10\t\n    11\tv2 answers council round 40 (`codex-r40.md`):\n    12\t- blind reading rules, an omitted material fact counted;\n    13\t- all Part C comparisons read;\n    14\t- the pass line stated as this probe's tolerance;\n    15\t- completeness required;\n    16\t- the sealed request last;\n    17\t- a schedule proved against the real reservations;\n    18\t- request-time checks;\n    19\t- a full $0 rehearsal.\n    20\t\n    21\tv3 answers round 40b (`codex-r40b.md`):\n    22\t- the targets' sources completed against the stored accepted retries (e3768 for the signed agreement; e41 and e120 for the Kyber\n    23\t  delay; the AMD entries), with a `partial` list;\n    24\t- misattribution counted by claim;\n    25\t- a material fact unsupported in all three draws treated as omitted;\n    26\t- Part C reads what every answer says and attributes;\n    27\t- a refused v7 control answer is still read;\n    28\t- the budget claim corrected;\n    29\t- the stops rehearsed.\n    30\t\n    31\tv4 answers round 40c (`codex-r40c.md`):\n    32\t- each evidence target's `required` claim and `optional` details;\n    33\t- class precedence;\n    34\t- Part C loss counted by claim;\n    35\t- quotes of shared sources in the packets;\n    36\t- one ordered verdict.\n    37\t\n    38\t## 1. What it decides\n    39\t\n    40\t| Question | Part |\n    41\t|---|---|\n    42\t| Q1. Does the provider accept judging-v12's format on a real request, the largest of the five archives included, and on an empty list? | A |\n    43\t| Q2. On the requests the open format let the model get wrong, does it now state each fact and cite a listed source for it, without a wrong listed id in its place, and without dropping a material fact? | B |\n    44\t| Q3. On ordinary requests, does the closed format change what the judge cites or concludes, beyond its own variation under the open format? | C |\n    45\t\n    46\t## 2. The sends, in this order\n    47\t\n    48\t1. **A1:** old-1 call 5652, the largest stored request of the five archives (451 evidence ids). Its `cites_views` is empty, so it\n    49\t   also exercises `maxItems: 0`.\n    50\t2. **A0:** old-3 call 69, a request with an empty theme list (`theme_pushes` with `maxItems: 0`); under $0.001.\n    51\t3. **Part B:** the 16 distinct refused requests, 3 sends each under v12's format.\n    52\t   - control-1's 8941 is 8938's retry: one request, both attempts' bad ids targeted.\n    53\t   - linked-1's 7 requests keep their stored judging-v8 text; only the answer format changes. That makes them a format probe on\n    54\t     those texts. No v8-based version is built.\n    55\t4. **Part C:** 12 matched comparisons, one per (source, question) of the refused set. Each is the same question's accepted\n    56\t   first-attempt request in the same archive with the closest evidence count; ties go to the nearest call on either side, which is\n    57\t   what `probe_plan.py` does.\n    58\t   - Each comparison is 3 sends under v12's format and 3 under judging-v7's open format (the fresh control).\n    59\t   - Comparisons run cheapest first. Within one comparison the six sends run one after another.\n    60\t   - The 16 refused requests map to 12 (source, question) pairs. The four duplicates are dropped to fit the ceiling, so every\n    61\t     question is covered once per source.\n    62\t5. **A2,** last and only if the headroom then covers its reservation ($0.0824): the sealed D358 run's call 6918 (647 ids) with v12's\n    63\t   format built from its lists. It is a size check on an older request text. A 200 shows that a request this size fits; a 400\n    64\t   establishes an enum limit only if the provider's error says so. Its answer is not read.\n    65\t\n    66\t**Start rule** (proved at $0 with `budget_replay.llm_estimate`):\n    67\t- Only one Part C comparison runs at a time.\n    68\t- It starts only when the ceiling minus spent minus reserved covers the sum of its six first attempts' reservations.\n    69\t- On the stored-token estimate all 12 start: lowest margin $0.037; expected core spend $0.347.\n    70\t- If every send costs 30% more than stored, only 10 start in this order: the 11th needs $0.136 with $0.107 left.\n    71\t- A retry reserves again, so an admitted comparison can still stop incomplete.\n    72\t- A comparison not started, or stopped, makes Part C incomplete, and the outcome inconclusive.\n    73\t\n    74\tEach part's sends run at most 4 at a time. Every send gets its own archive (per part, request, format and draw), so `model.call`\n    75\tnever answers a draw from an earlier draw: every draw is a fresh provider call, counted at the transport.\n    76\t\n    77\tA transport error is recorded. The budget transport retries a 429 or 5xx as it does in production, and settles an error at its\n    78\treservation.\n    79\t\n    80\t## 3. Reading rule (frozen)\n    81\t\n    82\t### Checks on every answer\n    83\tEvery answer is checked as at request time, with a harness check proved equal to `check_answer` on fixtures and on the stored\n    84\tanswers (§4):\n    85\t- membership against the request's lists;\n    86\t- the rung range from the request's ladder line;\n    87\t- first-judgement and changed against the request's \"[Previous conclusion …]\" line;\n    88\t- non-empty stance fields;\n    89\t- duplicate theme pushes.\n    90\t\n    91\tThe archive's final ledger state is not used: it falsely refuses stored answers such as 8834 and 8851 (Codex r40).\n    92\t\n    93\t### Part B (48 answers)\n    94\tEach answer is read against `probe-targets.json`.\n    95\t- **Evidence targets.** One class each, judged by the claim each cited or pushed entry is used for:\n    96\t  - *intended*: the claim is stated, an entry in `sources` is used for it, and no other entry is used for it without carrying it;\n    97\t  - *unsupported*: stated, with no entry in `sources`. An entry in `partial` alone leaves the exact claim unsupported, but is not a\n    98\t    wrong attribution;\n    99\t  - *misattributed*: an entry is used for the claim while its quote does not carry it. This counts even if the entry supports a\n   100\t    different claim in the same answer, or a correct source is also cited;\n   101\t  - *omitted*: the claim is not stated.\n   102\t  - The class is judged on the target's `required` claim against `sources`. An `optional` detail stated without its own source is\n   103\t    unsupported for that detail only, recorded, and does not change the class.\n   104\t  - When more than one class applies, misattributed comes first, then intended, then unsupported, then omitted. A wrong source with\n   105\t    no correct one is misattributed.\n   106\t  A `markers` search in the answer's text flags the reader's attention; the hand reading decides.\n   107\t- **Placement targets.**\n   108\t  - *correct*: the id appears only in its own field;\n   109\t  - *absent*: not named;\n   110\t  - a substitute evidence id carrying no claim the answer states is *misattributed*.\n   111\t- **Ambiguous targets** (two acceptable sources, or an unclear fact) are reported and count neither way.\n   112\t- **A second, blind reader** (Codex) reads the 48 against the frozen targets. A disagreement goes to a third, source-backed read whose\n   113\t  class decides.\n   114\t\n   115\t### Part C (12 comparisons, all 72 answers read)\n   116\t- Every answer is read in full: its reference, implied outcome, reasons, and the claim each cited or pushed source is used for,\n   117\t  shared sources included.\n   118\t- The numbers only order the reading:\n   119\t  - the sources cited by at least 2 of 3 answers in one arm and at most 1 of 3 in the other;\n   120\t  - any v12 rung outside the range of the v7 rungs.\n   121\t- A v7 answer the request-time check refuses is still read as an answer, and its refusal is recorded (it is the failure the closed\n   122\t  format removes). A comparison is complete with its 3 + 3 answers.\n   123\t\n   124\tA **material harm** is any of these, repeated (in at least 2 of 3 v12 answers and at most 1 of 3 v7 answers), counted by claim, not by\n   125\tsource id:\n   126\t- (a) a claim that moves the forecast or the reference, which at least 2 of 3 v7 answers state with a listed source carrying it (any\n   127\t  such source: one control citing e195 and another e669 for the $393 billion reference count as two), and which at least 2 of 3 v12\n   128\t  answers do not state with a carrying source;\n   129\t- (b) a source used by at least 2 of 3 v12 answers for a claim its quote does not carry, for example \"Bloomberg supplied the $390\n   130\t  billion forecast\" where Bloomberg's entry gives $393 billion as the market's estimate;\n   131\t- (c) a changed reference or implied outcome whose stated support is a citation of kind (a) or (b);\n   132\t- (d) a v12 rung outside the v7 range whose reasons trace to (a), (b) or (c).\n   133\t\n   134\tA difference that is not repeated, or whose cause cannot be read, is **unresolved**.\n   135\t\n   136\t### Outcome (registered; proposed tolerances for this probe, not historical rates)\n   137\tOne verdict, taken from the first rule that applies:\n   138\t1. **Not ready (format):** A1 or A0 is rejected or returns a format-invalid answer.\n   139\t2. **Not ready (confirmed failure):** any of\n   140\t   - a v12 answer refused by the request-time check;\n   141\t   - more than 2 of 48 Part B answers with a confirmed misattribution;\n   142\t   - a confirmed material loss in Part B;\n   143\t   - a confirmed material harm in Part C.\n   144\t\n   145\t   A confirmed failure stands even when the run is incomplete.\n   146\t3. **Inconclusive (incomplete):** a budget stop, a missing Part B answer, or a Part C comparison not started or interrupted.\n   147\t4. **Inconclusive (unresolved):** an unresolved material loss in Part B, or an unresolved Part C difference that would be material if\n   148\t   confirmed.\n   149\t5. **Pass (\"ready to propose adoption\"):** otherwise.\n   150\t\n   151\tA2, sent, skipped or rejected, never changes the verdict; it is reported. The conditions behind these rules:\n   152\t- **Pass,** when every condition holds:\n   153\t  - Q1: A1 and A0 return 200 with format-valid answers;\n   154\t  - all 48 Part B answers and all 12 Part C comparisons (72 answers) are complete;\n   155\t  - no v12 answer is refused by the request-time check;\n   156\t  - in Part B, at most 2 of 48 answers have a confirmed misattribution (an answer counts once), with the number of requests affected\n   157\t    and any repetition reported;\n   158\t  - no confirmed material loss in Part B: a material target omitted or unsupported in all 3 draws, which the stored accepted v7\n   159\t    answer to the same request stated and supported;\n   160\t  - no confirmed material harm in Part C.\n   161\t- **Inconclusive:**\n   162\t  - a budget stop, a missing answer, a comparison not started or interrupted;\n   163\t  - an unresolved material loss in Part B: a material target omitted or unsupported in all 3 draws where no stored accepted v7 answer\n   164\t    to that request kept it, as in control-1's 8938, whose retry also dropped 85.4%;\n   165\t  - an unresolved Part C difference that would be material if confirmed.\n   166\t\n   167\tThe outcome is computed by code (`probe_read.py`) from the read classes; the rehearsal exercises it (§4).\n   168\t- **Not ready:** any other failure of the pass conditions, with its reason.\n   169\t- Every outcome goes to Alex; adoption is his decision.\n   170\t\n   171\t## 4. Harness and the $0 rehearsal before the send\n   172\t\n   173\t`probe.py`, harness-only:\n   174\t- it reads `probe-plan.json` and builds each request with `model.build_request`, from poc-v121's setting and v12's format (or v7's\n   175\t  for the control);\n   176\t- it sends through `budget_replay.BudgetTransport` on a ledger at $0.50, in the order and under the start rule of §2;\n   177\t- each answer goes through `model.call`'s format check and the request-time check;\n   178\t- each answer is written to `probe-answers.jsonl` with its part, request, format, draw, the request sha, the cost and the transport's\n   179\t  call number.\n   180\t- `probe_read.py` builds the reading packets:\n   181\t  - Part B by target, with marker flags;\n   182\t  - Part C by comparison: all six answers in full, the quote of every source any of them cites (shared ones included), and the\n   183\t    symmetric-difference sources marked.\n   184\t- `probe_read.py` also computes the one verdict of §3 from the read classes.\n   185\t\n   186\t**The $0 rehearsal** uses the real budget transport with the provider stubbed underneath (`model.openai_transport` replaced), on a\n   187\tledger file of its own. It must show:\n   188\t- every scheduled send reaches the stub, with a count equal to the plan: 2 + 1 for A, 48 for B, 72 for C;\n   189\t- each request's bytes: system and user equal the stored ones, the format strict and equal to `schema_for('judging-v12', lists)` (or\n   190\t  v7's), the model settings as poc-v121's;\n   191\t- three fresh stub calls per draw set;\n   192\t- the request-time check equals `check_answer` on a ledger fixture whose state is known, accepts every stored committed answer of the\n   193\t  planned requests, and refuses the stored refused ones on their ids;\n   194\t- the stub's valid answer, a format-invalid answer, an HTTP 400 and a 5xx followed by success each take their path;\n   195\t- only one Part C comparison runs at a time;\n   196\t- a ceiling set low blocks a Part C start, and the outcome is \"inconclusive\", never \"pass\";\n   197\t- a retry exhausts the remaining headroom inside an admitted comparison, which stops it; the outcome is \"inconclusive\";\n   198\t- the outcome code's verdicts:\n   199\t  - three Part B answers for control-1's 8938 that state 85.4% with no source are an unresolved material loss, so \"inconclusive\"\n   200\t    (8938 has no stored accepted v7 answer);\n   201\t  - three answers for control-1's 8807 that state the $393 billion reference with no source are a confirmed material loss, so \"not\n   202\t    ready\" (its stored accepted retry 8809 cites e195 and e669);\n   203\t  - three misattributions are \"not ready\";\n   204\t  - a clean set is \"pass\";\n   205\t  - an A1 rejection is \"not ready (format)\", even though it also leaves an answer missing;\n   206\t  - a confirmed misattribution excess with Part C incomplete is \"not ready\";\n   207\t  - an unresolved material Part C difference with everything else clean is \"inconclusive\";\n   208\t  - A2 skipped, and A2 rejected, each leave a clean core \"pass\";\n   209\t- the Part B packet for 8938 flags a stub answer that drops \"85.4\".\n   210\t\n   211\tA mutant, Part B sent with the open format, is caught by the byte check.\n2: \"frozen\": \"2026-11-22, before any probe send; read by Claude from the stored refused answers and their requests (probe-plan.json). Amended once before any send (council round 40b): sources completed against the stored accepted retries; a `partial` list (entries that support only a looser version of the claim); misattribution counted by the claim a source is used for. Not edited after the first send. Second amendment before any send (council round 40c): each evidence target names its `required` claim, judged against `sources`, and any `optional` details with their own sources; a stated optional detail without its source is unsupported for that detail only and does not change the target's class; precedence misattributed > intended > unsupported > omitted.\",\n4:  \"evidence\": \"per target, by the claim each cited or pushed entry is used for: intended (the claim is stated and an entry in `sources` is cited or pushed for it, and no other entry is used for that claim without carrying it); unsupported (stated, with no entry in `sources`; an entry in `partial` alone leaves the exact claim unsupported but is not a wrong attribution); misattributed (an entry is used for the claim while its quote does not carry it, a `near_misses` entry included, even if a correct source is also cited); omitted (not stated)\",\n35:     \"sources\": [\n50:     \"why\": \"e88 is an unlisted id the request names in 'same claim as e88' on e42 and e250; the forecast (rung 2) rests on this fact; e41, e42, e120 and e250 each report the SemiAnalysis delay to 2028; NVIDIA's denials (e40, e111, e121, e167, e214, e251) are counterevidence, not sources for this claim\",\n52:     \"required\": \"SemiAnalysis reports Kyber NVL144 delayed to 2028\",\n53:     \"optional\": [\n56:       \"sources\": [\n75:     \"sources\": [\n99:     \"required\": \"NVIDIA has entered (signed) a definitive agreement to acquire Hugging Face\",\n100:     \"optional\": [\n103:       \"sources\": [\n137:     \"sources\": [\n152:     \"required\": \"NVIDIA warned infrastructure shortages (land, power) could delay deployments\",\n153:     \"optional\": []\n165:     \"fact\": \"ambiguous: a supporting detail of the reported NVIDIA-OpenAI financing talks (e1380, pushed toward_first but not cited, is the likeliest)\",\n167:     \"sources\": [\n173:     \"ambiguous\": true,\n175:     \"why\": \"e1382 is not in the request; same article as e1380, e1381 (cited), e1385; reported as ambiguous, it counts neither way\",\n177:     \"required\": \"ambiguous\",\n178:     \"optional\": []\n192:     \"sources\": [\n205:     \"required\": \"NVIDIA expects Vera deployed by every major hyperscaler, with shipments underway to lead partners\",\n206:     \"optional\": []\n220:     \"sources\": [\n231:     \"required\": \"the market reference of about $393 billion FY2027 revenue\",\n232:     \"optional\": []\n246:     \"sources\": [\n256:     \"required\": \"Zacks consensus FY2027 revenue growth of 85.4%\",\n257:     \"optional\": []\n263:     \"fact\": \"ambiguous: an unquantified downside risk (Eisman's price-war warning in e3110, or Burry's customer concentration in e3112)\",\n265:     \"sources\": [\n271:     \"ambiguous\": true,\n275:     \"required\": \"ambiguous\",\n276:     \"optional\": []\n290:     \"sources\": [\n305:     \"required\": \"AMD competition in data-center CPUs (share gains or performance claims)\",\n306:     \"optional\": []\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '10756,10772p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; sed -n '448,460p' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md; ls -lt docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe*\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '10756,10772p' docs/DECISIONS-log.md; sed -n '448,460p' docs/CURRENT_STATE.md; ls -lt docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe*\"","aggregated_output":"## D715 · 2026-11-22 · Alex approves $0.50 for the paid acceptance step of judging-v12\n\n- **The question:** \"引用格式的新版本已经做好，所有不花钱的验证都通过了。要不要花一点钱实测？实测这样做：先发最大的一次请求和一次名单为空的请求，确认服务商接受这个格式；再把当初被退回的 17 个请求和 17 个正常请求用新版本重发，人工对照原文看模型有没有选对证据。每个请求发一次，约 0.10 美元；各发三次看稳不稳，约 0.30 美元。发之前我会先和审查员定好怎么读、怎么判。\"\n  Options: 0.5 美元 (recommended: three sends per request with a margin; a stop above $0.50; the reading rule agreed with the council\n  before the send; Claude reads the results); 0.15 美元 (one send per request); 先不花 (stop; poc-v118 stays the product).\n- **Alex's answer** (2026-11-22): \"0.5 美元 (推荐)\".\n- **Next:** the probe design and its reading rule through the council at $0, the harness dry-run at $0, then the send under a $0.50\n  reservation ledger.\n**The one next task (D714, 2026-11-21): Alex's choice on the paid acceptance step for judging-v12.** The step: the largest stored\nrequest and an empty-list request for provider acceptance, then the 17 stored refused requests and a matched set of accepted ones,\nread beside their sources.\n- **Opened** by Alex (D712) and designed through council round 38 (D713).\n- **Built:** judging-v12 is judging-v7 whose four answer id fields take only the ids the request lists; poc-v121 is poc-v118 with it.\n  Uncommitted.\n- **Passed every registered $0 check** (D714; `research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/RESULT.md`):\n  - old-2 replayed under v12 equals old-2;\n  - all 5,391 valid stored answers fit;\n  - all 17 refused ones are excluded.\n\nBefore it, the pilot of the paid whole-window comparison (D711, `research/2026-11-21-whole-window/PILOT-RESULT.md`) closed:\n- **Verdict:** inconclusive (D711). control-1 stopped on 09-08 on a double refusal: two one-character evidence-id copy errors. linked-1\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff    11455 Nov 22 00:41 docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe-targets.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff  1906932 Nov 22 00:36 docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe-plan.json\n-rw-r--r--@ 1 lchingen  staff     7284 Nov 22 00:36 docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe_plan.py\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,30p;168,193p' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; tail -n 3 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_6","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"sed -n '1,30p;168,193p' docs/prd/10-filing-phase.md; tail -n 3 docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md\"","aggregated_output":"# Core PRD for the next phase: filing must recognise indirect relations the way an analyst does\n\n> Status: in progress (opened 2026-11-04). Alex: \"你把这个写好成下一阶段核心PRD然后不要drift, 把所有需要的context 全部充分记录，每次开始前都需要revisit, 然后开始做\".\n> This page is the single source for this phase. In a conflict: Alex's words → `docs/DECISIONS.md` → this page → the other design documents. This page's\n> conclusions, evidence, constraints, measuring method and process are not rewritten to follow test results;\n> test results go into `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/log.md`, and changing this page first needs Alex's word.\n> Amended 2026-11-04 (Alex replied \"go\" to the proposed amendment; D360): §5.2 drops \"also file under the other party's question\" and puts two\n> sentences in its place, one on choosing and one on splitting; §6's decision rule is rewritten. How it came about:\n> `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/prd-amendment-proposal.md` and `log.md` rows 11–16.\n> 2026-11-05 (D368): translated into English on Alex's word (\"不，用英文吧\"); §4 corrected to name the frozen standard's version 5 and §5 given a status line, on his delegation (\"你要来帮我看到底做不做\").\n\n## 0. Checklist before every start (Alex: \"每次开始前都需要revisit\")\n\nBefore starting any step, finish these in order; if one cannot be done, do not start:\n\n1. Read §§1–8 of this page in full; read the last three rows of `log.md`, and confirm where the previous step stopped and why.\n2. Check against §3, \"not in scope\": what this step does is not in that table. If it is in the table, stop and take it to Alex.\n3. Check against §4, \"constraints\": this step changes nothing frozen; a change to the frozen extraction prompt is the one place §5 names, and Alex's\n   word for it is already given.\n4. If this step costs money: its predictions and stop conditions are written down and frozen as §7 says (with their sha256 recorded beside them); the\n   requests are rebuilt byte for byte as §6 says; the control is re-sent the same day.\n5. What goes to Alex: one conclusion, one recommendation, one test, after §7's rounds of review; no menu of options; in plain words (the opening of\n   AGENTS, \"Explain and answer as to a sixteen-year-old\").\n\n## 1. Goal (end to end)\n\nEach question's judgement must receive the facts that can change its answer; facts that no question receives, those that bear on no question, must\nnot be piled into some one question. What is measured is the final judgement (the frozen judgement ruler, reader B, at the window end 2026-07-14), not\nany one step's own score.\n\n## 7. Process (no drift)\n\n- **One recommendation and one test at a time** (AGENTS §7.3, Alex: \"就测试一种，一次\"): write the design first and put it through rounds of review (own\n  checks, Codex read-only, a reader who did not write it reading the raw records) until a round finds nothing serious; write down and freeze the\n  predictions and stop conditions; test once; if it does not match, stop and take it to Alex (D355: \"如果有什么不符合hypothesis 的地方你需要终止然后和我说我们重新评估\").\n- **A review's report is a lead**: each finding counts only once it is checked against the records (AGENTS §1).\n- **A prompt audit before any prompt change** (`.claude/skills/prompt-audit/SKILL.md`): check the whole request against the standard sentence by\n  sentence, in both directions.\n- **Every step goes into `log.md`**: what was done, what came of it, the files; mistakes and overturned results stay in it too.\n- **Do not repeat what was ruled out** (§3).\n\n## 8. Steps and where we are\n\n| # | Step | Output | Status |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| 1 | Design: the classes of indirect relation (a closed set + examples from other industries), how to file when a fact measures both sides, deleting the fallback; checked against the standard sentence by sentence; length before and after | `docs/research/2026-11-04-filing-end-to-end/design-links.md` | Done (draft 3, v74l / poc-v115) |\n| 2 | Checks at no cost: a sample answer written by the new rule goes through every code check; the new rule's text goes through the prompt audit | Same as above | Done |\n| 3 | Review rounds (Codex, independent readers, own), until nothing serious remains | `review-links-*.md` | Done (Codex 7 rounds, independent readers 3 times; round 7 found nothing serious) |\n| 4 | Draw and freeze the held-out set; write down and freeze this test's predictions and decision rule | `heldout.json`, `predictions-links.md` | Done (sha256 recorded for both) |\n| 5 | Test once: development set + held-out set, the new rule and the same-day control 3 times each | `answers-links.json`, `log.md` | Done (2026-11-04): failed: facts that matter reaching the right question, development set +7 (p 0.26); every other condition passed |\n| 6 | If passed: to Alex, to decide whether to run three 14-day end-to-end draws; if failed: stop, to Alex | `design-links.md` §8 | Stopped, to Alex |\n| 7 | (D361, Alex: \"按照你的提以来，但是你一定是自己反思多轮之后才给出的行动\") Measure the ceiling first: hand the source passages the gold cites straight to the frozen judgement; the custom-chip, operating-margin and capital-spending questions judged 3 times each at the window end, the custom-chip question as it was 3 times as the control; the fallback sentence is not deleted for now | `reflection-v74l.md`, `oracle-design.md` | Done: operating margin grounded 3/3, capital spending 2/3, custom chips 0/3 (the gap is in interpretation); the next step waits for Alex |\n| 8 | (D362, Alex: \"你继续啊不要scope drift and strongly follow evidence of your discovery and learning\") Two small changes where facts are not delivered, one at a time: ① when a quote is rewritten, code matches it back to the source sentence (changing nothing the model sees; verified by replaying the archive); ② a figure question's description states which figures it is derived from by definition (first sent 3 times each on the article that motivated it) | `delivery-fixes.md` | Stopped: an independent check overturned the first change's code (it would take in wrong figures); the second failed its trial send (1/3). The root: the signed standard's §5.3 does not keep two key facts, treating them as \"a restatement of known facts\" (proposal 6, awaiting approval); to Alex |\n| 9 | **Historical; superseded by D370.** (D363, Alex: \"乙\") At coverage start, record each question's starting figure once from the company's latest earnings report; the daily path still takes no restatements: design, rounds of self-checks and independent checks, validated first on the archive in the simplest way | `baseline-design.md` | Validated on two questions: the frozen extraction does not read the report's tables (0/3); with each question reading the report once on its own, the operating-margin question read its starting figure 2/3 and the capital-spending question 3/3, and the judgement then judged right (2/3, 3/3), about 2.5 cents. All 22 questions tested once (2026-11-05, Alex: \"你充分验证\"; files chosen by code, a same-day control, about $0.43): v10 and v12 judged right 9/9 each; no question already judged right turned wrong; but 5 of the 53 figures read were other quantities (the Vera CPU question and the Blackwell and Rubin question took a larger or neighbouring revenue line), so it failed condition 3, written beforehand. The model itself pointed to the reading instructions' sentence \"write the lines it is computed from, or the line the report uses for it\"; stopped, to Alex. Alex: \"改\"; only this sentence was changed (\"write only the lines it is computed from, or the same quantity under another name; never a broader line or a line next to it\"), tried on 4 questions first, then tested on all 22 (about $0.36): all three conditions passed: v10 and v12 9/9 each, no question judged right turned wrong, and all 46 figures were the questions' own quantities. Checked after an independent reader's challenge: the new sentence made the reading miss the capital-spending line in 3 of 12 reads, and it had been tested only on the one May report; the fourth version (a line-by-line re-check after writing) removed too much and failed; after a census of every failure trace (Alex: \"我需要你深度看完所有失败trace给我准信\"), the third version with the repaired quote check was chosen (D365): 0 wrong figures on the held-out August report; built into the production system (poc-v116; the $0 checks and the tests all pass). The full acceptance, three 14-day draws (Alex: \"跑验收\"; a same-day control; about $4.79): all passed: operating margin and capital spending judged right 3/3 each (the control never judged them), 53 against 45 in total (of 57); for the China-share question, the only one two fewer, both readers found the starting figures did not lead it astray. Alex: \"都做\": poc-v116 became the default (D366); the code was committed and a PR opened |\n\n## 9. Alex's own words on this matter (in time order)\n| 39 | 11-05 | 第 3 步：做进正式系统（设计四张表，Codex 审 3 轮：第 1 轮 4 条严重、第 2 轮 2 条严重，都改；第 3 轮无严重问题） | 建成 `baseline.run` + poc-v116 + baseline-v3 提示词文件；$0 核对：44 份请求和验证时逐字节相同，3 次存下的回答走正式代码写出的记录完全一样，第一天判断正好判这些题，网页从开始跟踪那天可见；新测试 12 条、6 个弄坏版本都抓出、全套 272 条通过；设计页和 PRD 00/03/04/05/06 更新，`docs/check.py` 通过 | 交 Alex：要不要跑 14 天三遍完整验收（约 5 美元） |\n| 40 | 11-05 | Alex：\"跑验收\"。14 天三遍完整验收：poc-v116（开始跟踪时读财报）三遍、当天重跑 poc-v108 三遍作对照，冻结尺子打分（事先锁定 `acceptance-design.md`）；电脑中途在电池上睡了约 5 小时，6 遍被暂停，插电后自己接着跑完 | **全过**：v10、v12 各 3/3（对照从没判过）；合计 53 对 45（满分 57，+8）；唯一少两次的 v17（0/3 对 2/3）两人都认定不是起点数：同一份抽取请求，新配置两遍碰巧留下\"中国份额归零\"那句，对照没留；约 4.79 美元 | 交 Alex：poc-v116 是否成为默认 |\n| 41 | 11-05 | Alex：\"都做\"（poc-v116 设成默认；提交代码、开 PR）。默认配置改成 poc-v116，默认的条目数据库换成带财报网页原文的那一份（旧的没有原文，新默认会在它上面拒跑）；测试按用户的用法补上：不给种子题就拒绝，给了就先读财报再跑第一天 | 测试全过，5 个弄坏的版本都抓出；配置的设置和验收三遍记下的校验码一致（只改了配置里的注释）；花钱前的检查脚本在新配置的运行数据上照常跑完，但不复查读财报那一步的引用检查（记为未补的缺口）；D366 | 提交、开 PR；下一类问题等 Alex |\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '162,182p;253,288p'; nl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '268,291p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe-targets.json | sed -n '210,235p'\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/opt/homebrew/bin/zsh -lc \"nl -ba src/hivemind/model.py | sed -n '162,182p;253,288p'; nl -ba clean-arch/e2e-comparison-2026-11-13/budget_replay.py | sed -n '268,291p'; nl -ba docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/probe-targets.json | sed -n '210,235p'\"","aggregated_output":"   162\t        except urllib.error.HTTPError as error:\n   163\t            body_bytes = error.read()\n   164\t            body_text = body_bytes.decode('utf-8', 'replace' if max_attempts == 1 else 'ignore')\n   165\t            last_http = (error.code, body_text, base64.b64encode(body_bytes).decode('ascii'))\n   166\t            last = f'HTTP {error.code}: {body_text[:600]}'\n   167\t            if error.code in (400, 401, 403, 404):\n   168\t                failure = TransportError(last)\n   169\t                failure.response_body = body_text\n   170\t                failure.response_body_base64 = last_http[2]\n   171\t                failure.http_status = error.code\n   172\t                raise failure\n   173\t        except (urllib.error.URLError, TimeoutError, ConnectionError, OSError, http.client.HTTPException) as error:   # a dropped or truncated response is retried like a network error\n   174\t            last = repr(error)[:200]\n   175\t            last_http = None   # the final failure describes the last attempt only\n   176\t        if max_attempts == 3 or attempt + 1 < max_attempts:\n   177\t            time.sleep(5 * (attempt + 1))\n   178\t    failure = TransportError(last or 'no answer')\n   179\t    if last_http:\n   180\t        failure.http_status, failure.response_body, failure.response_body_base64 = last_http\n   181\t    raise failure\n   182\t\n   253\tdef call(archive, cfg, setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, purpose, *, transport=None):\n   254\t    provider = cfg.provider\n   255\t    request = build_request(setting, system, user, schema, schema_name, provider)\n   256\t    request_json, sha = request_identity(request)\n   257\t    hit = archive.lookup(sha)\n   258\t    prompt_chars = len(system) + len(user)\n   259\t    if hit:\n   260\t        call_id, answer_json, _, input_tokens, output_tokens = hit\n   261\t        return Answer(json.loads(answer_json), call_id, sha, True, prompt_chars, input_tokens or 0, output_tokens or 0, 0.0)\n   262\t    started = time.time()\n   263\t    response = (transport or openai_transport)(provider, request)\n   264\t    seconds = round(time.time() - started, 1)\n   265\t    try:\n   266\t        content = response['choices'][0]['message']['content']\n   267\t        data = json.loads(content)\n   268\t    except (KeyError, IndexError, TypeError, json.JSONDecodeError) as error:\n   269\t        archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   270\t                       request_sha256=sha + ':malformed:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   271\t                       response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=None, prompt_chars=prompt_chars,\n   272\t                       input_tokens=0, output_tokens=0, cost_usd=0.0, seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   273\t        raise SchemaError(f'malformed answer: {error}')\n   274\t    errors = check_schema(data, schema)\n   275\t    usage = response.get('usage') or {}\n   276\t    input_tokens = int(usage.get('prompt_tokens') or 0)\n   277\t    output_tokens = int(usage.get('completion_tokens') or 0)\n   278\t    cached_tokens = min(input_tokens, int((usage.get('prompt_tokens_details') or {}).get('cached_tokens') or 0))\n   279\t    price_in, price_out = PRICES.get(setting.model, (0.0, 0.0))\n   280\t    cost = round((input_tokens - cached_tokens) / 1e6 * price_in + cached_tokens / 1e6 * price_in * CACHED_INPUT_SHARE + output_tokens / 1e6 * price_out, 6)\n   281\t    call_id = archive.record(purpose=purpose, config_version=cfg.version, config_checksum=cfg.checksum, model=setting.model,\n   282\t                             request_sha256=sha if not errors else sha + ':schema:' + uuid.uuid4().hex[:8], request_json=request_json,\n   283\t                             response_json=json.dumps(response)[:200000], answer_json=json.dumps(data, ensure_ascii=False),\n   284\t                             prompt_chars=prompt_chars, input_tokens=input_tokens, output_tokens=output_tokens, cost_usd=cost,\n   285\t                             seconds=seconds, created_at=time.strftime('%Y-%m-%dT%H:%M:%S'))\n   286\t    if errors:\n   287\t        raise SchemaError('; '.join(errors[:5]))\n   288\t    return Answer(data, call_id, sha, False, prompt_chars, input_tokens, output_tokens, cost)\n   268\t    def __call__(self, *args):\n   269\t        if len(args) == 1:\n   270\t            return self._jev(args[0])\n   271\t        provider, request = args\n   272\t        for attempt in range(3):\n   273\t            estimate = llm_estimate(request)\n   274\t            if not self.ledger.reserve(estimate):\n   275\t                raise model.TransportError('the shared budget ceiling would be passed: not sent')\n   276\t            try:\n   277\t                response = model.openai_transport(provider, request, max_attempts=1)\n   278\t            except model.TransportError as error:\n   279\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   280\t                status = getattr(error, 'http_status', None)\n   281\t                if status in CLIENT_ERRORS or attempt == 2 or (status is not None and status != 429 and status < 500):\n   282\t                    raise\n   283\t                self.sleep(5 * (attempt + 1))\n   284\t                continue\n   285\t            except Exception:\n   286\t                self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate)\n   287\t                raise\n   288\t            cost = llm_cost(response, request)\n   289\t            self.ledger.settle(estimate, estimate if cost is None else cost)\n   290\t            return response\n   291\t        raise model.TransportError('no answer after three attempts')\n   210\t  {\n   211\t   \"key\": \"control-1:8807\",\n   212\t   \"view\": \"v14\",\n   213\t   \"targets\": [\n   214\t    {\n   215\t     \"kind\": \"evidence\",\n   216\t     \"bad\": \"e393\",\n   217\t     \"role\": \"cite and push toward_first\",\n   218\t     \"fact\": \"the market reference: about $393 billion FY2027 revenue\",\n   219\t     \"passage\": \"The market reference is about $393 billion for FY2027, which sits in rung 3.\",\n   220\t     \"sources\": [\n   221\t      \"e195\",\n   222\t      \"e669\"\n   223\t     ],\n   224\t     \"near_misses\": [],\n   225\t     \"material\": true,\n   226\t     \"markers\": [\n   227\t      \"393\"\n   228\t     ],\n   229\t     \"why\": \"e393 is not in the request; the model wrote the reference amount as an id; e195 (Bloomberg) and e669 (Wall Street average) carry $393 billion\",\n   230\t     \"partial\": [],\n   231\t     \"required\": \"the market reference of about $393 billion FY2027 revenue\",\n   232\t     \"optional\": []\n   233\t    }\n   234\t   ]\n   235\t  },\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_8","type":"agent_message","text":"**NOT READY.** Part B can still pass when none of the three answers gives a correct source for a material claim.\n\n1. **Count material loss separately from wrong attribution.** For `8807`, suppose two answers give the $393B reference with a wrong source and the third omits it. The two wrong attributions are within tolerance, and the material-loss rule only counts answers labelled omitted or unsupported. Record whether each draw gives valid support separately from its error label. This case should be **not ready** because the saved retry supports the claim. [Part B outcome](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:139)\n\n2. **Apply Part C’s claim-based count to wrong attributions too.** Rule (b) still requires the same source to be used twice. If two v12 answers use different sources for the same incorrect $390B market reference, and both sources actually say $393B, count that as repeated harm. [Part C harm rules](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:124)\n\n3. **Require successful A1 and A0 results in the ordered verdict.** If A1 times out after retries, it has neither a format rejection nor a valid answer. The ordered incomplete rule does not cover that case, so a clean B and C could fall through to pass. Add the missing required A result to the incomplete rule and rehearse it separately from an explicit format rejection. [Ordered verdict](/Users/lchingen/hivemind/docs/research/2026-11-21-citation-lists/PROBE-DESIGN.md:136)"}}
